    {
      "title": "Primitive Obsession and Cohesion",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Primitive Obsession and Cohesion",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Primitive Obsession",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Primitive Obsession== = `String`, `int`, `double` standing in for money, email, phone, status code",
                "Validation and behavior {red:scatter} across every caller",
                "Fix: ==Replace Primitive with Value Object==: **immutable**, validates in its constructor",
                "`Money(amount, currency)` owns `add()` and `format()`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "@dataclass(frozen=True)",
                "class Money:",
                "    amount: Decimal",
                "    currency: str",
                "    def __post_init__(self):",
                "        if self.amount < 0: raise ValueError",
                "    def add(self, o):",
                "        return Money(self.amount + o.amount, self.currency)"
              ],
              "note": "frozen = immutable; invalid state never exists"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Type Codes",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Type code",
                "Drives behavior?",
                "Fix"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`status = 2`, `\"paid\"`",
                  "No",
                  "==enum== or class: illegal values cannot compile"
                ],
                [
                  "`if kind == \"express\"` in many places",
                  "Yes",
                  "**Polymorphism**: State or Strategy"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Data Clumps",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Same 3 params travel together: `start`, `end`, `timezone`",
                "Fix: one ==parameter object== (`DateRange`)",
                "Bonus: shorter parameter lists"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Mistake",
              "text": "Wrapping **every** primitive in a class. Wrap only values with ==rules, invariants or behavior==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Refactoring to Strategy, State and Template Method",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Refactoring to Strategy, State and Template Method",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Conditional to Polymorphism",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Each switch branch becomes a ==subclass== of one interface; callers lose the switch",
                "{blue:Strategy}: client picks the algorithm, context delegates",
                "{green:State}: object changes behavior itself; replaces boolean flags"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Strategy vs State",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "interface ShippingCost { double cost(Order o); }",
                "class Express implements ShippingCost {...} // or Standard",
                "double total() { return shipping.cost(this); }",
                "class Pending implements OrderState {",
                "  public OrderState pay() { return new Paid(); }",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "Strategy delegates; State returns the next state"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Strategy",
                "State"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Class shape",
                  "Same",
                  "Same"
                ],
                [
                  "Chosen by",
                  "Client",
                  "Object itself"
                ],
                [
                  "Knows others",
                  "No",
                  "Yes, successors"
                ],
                [
                  "Swapped",
                  "By client, not by itself",
                  "Own transitions"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Template Method",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Template Method==: base class fixes the skeleton in a `final` method calling abstract steps",
                "Subclasses fill in steps like parse, validate, save; fits duplicated flows differing in few steps",
                "For runtime swapping or composition, use {blue:Strategy}."
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Strategy vs State?** Same shape; client picks Strategy, State switches itself to successors",
                "**Template Method vs Strategy?** Inheritance and fixed skeleton vs runtime swap and composition"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
